  "caption": "Quinn's first golf day in six months: three buckets, 300 swings, no warm-up. Next morning, back, elbow and shoulder all had opinions.\n\nThe golf swing is a fast twist repeated around a hundred times a round. If the hips and mid-back are stiff, the low back often takes up the slack, and a sudden jump in practice after a week at a desk adds to it.\n\nTips that may help: a ten-minute dynamic warm-up starting with short irons, daily hip and mid-back rotation, strength training twice a week, and building practice gradually with an easy grip, fitted clubs and a push cart.\n\nPain that lingers or gets worse, or any numbness or weakness, is worth getting checked. Easing off a sore elbow early is wise.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
